From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:51:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sysreset: psci: fall back to other drivers if the reset
 returns

The MSM8953 firmware returns from PSCI SYSTEM_RESET without resetting.
Reporting -EINPROGRESS stopped the walk, so the PS_HOLD driver that does
work was never tried.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/sysreset/sysreset_psci.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/sysreset/sysreset_psci.c b/drivers/sysreset/sysreset_psci.c
index 89b4f2dc..adf65cde 100644
--- a/drivers/sysreset/sysreset_psci.c
+++ b/drivers/sysreset/sysreset_psci.c
@@ -27,7 +27,12 @@ static int psci_sysreset_request(struct udevice *dev, enum sysreset_t type)
 		return -EPROTONOSUPPORT;
 	}
 
-	return -EINPROGRESS;
+	/*
+	 * SYSTEM_RESET and SYSTEM_OFF do not return on success. Some firmware
+	 * returns anyway without resetting, give the other sysreset drivers a
+	 * chance in that case.
+	 */
+	return -EIO;
 }
 
 static struct sysreset_ops psci_sysreset_ops = {
